  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Gustar",
    "@en": "Like"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "En inglés, quien siente el gusto es el sujeto: **I like coffee** equivale a «me gusta el café».",
     "@en": "In English, who feels the taste is the subject: **I like coffee** equals «I like coffee.»."
    },
    {
     "@es": "**I love** = me encanta. **I don't like** = no me gusta. **I hate** = odio. Para preguntar usamos el presente simple: **Do you like fish?** — **Yes, I do / No, I don't**.",
     "@en": "**I love** = I love it. **I don't like** = I don't like it. **I hate** = hate. To ask, we use the simple present: **Do you like fish?**-**Yes, I do / No, I don't**."
    }
   ]
  },
